Are multiple text colors in a single bundle also not supported?

In the example below, both sections are the same size (understandably, with current cosmic-text limitations).

But they are also both green, which I would hope would work.

```rust
use bevy::prelude::*;

fn main() {
    App::new()
        .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins)
        .add_systems(Startup, setup)
        .run();
}

fn setup(mut commands: Commands, asset_server: Res<AssetServer>) {
    // UI camera
    commands.spawn(Camera2dBundle::default());

    commands.spawn(TextBundle::from_sections([
        TextSection::new(
            "S1",
            TextStyle {
                font_size: 60.,
                color: Color::GREEN,
                font: asset_server.load("fonts/FiraSans-Bold.ttf"),
            },
        ),
        TextSection::new(
            "S2",
            TextStyle {
                font_size: 30.0,
                color: Color::RED,
                font: asset_server.load("fonts/FiraSans-Bold.ttf"),
            },
        ),
    ]));
}
```

@jackpot51 I will wait with doing optimization efforts from this, mostly since I believe there is a large chance of bugs with doing manual cache clearance at this point in time. 

For anyone wondering why this does not get merged, the current implementation of cosmic-text in bevy removes some functionality, and thus its controversial to add this. When the multi-font-size feature is implemented in cosmic-text ( current work here PR: https://github.com/pop-os/cosmic-text/pull/235)  there will be no reduction of functionality, and significant performance boost, along with support for more advanced text features such as ligatures and such. (feel free to correct me here)

I believe that this work, will make it easier to upstream text-editing widgets (looking at a current text-edit implementation: https://github.com/StaffEngineer/bevy_cosmic_edit).

